That's the Wizard's tower.  You can see him sleeping on the top level
if you have telepathy.  Anyway, go down a few more levels and you'll
find some way to get in.  (Hint: it's also in the middle of the screen.)

About your "bitch".  The priest doesn't have to be co-aligned for you
to get AC protection.  Also, a temple priest will become hostile after
you convert the altar.  To convert an altar, sacrifice something big.
If there is a priest-less altar, this will give you a handy altar to
get artifacts.

Anyway, the standard way to get AC bonus and your money back is to
give your golds to a non-co-aligned priest, convert the altar, and
then kill the now-hostile priest.  This way, you'll only lose
telepathy, so if you have an appropriate helmet/amulet/PYEC/something
else, you won't really lose anything.

Do *not* try to kill the priest before converting the altar, one, he
is peaceful and it's bad to attack a peaceful creature unless you are
chaotic, and two, his god will fight for him.  If you have all sorts
of resistances and reflection, it might be fun (you'll see the
"wide-range disintegration beam" (or something like that) and some
amusing messages from the other god).

